		)
		(uuid "1d3928bb-8afb-4aad-9537-40e17da1c143")
	)
	(text "1) RS485 BUS TERMINATION: ON THE LAST SLAVE DEVICE OF AN RS485 BUS DO NOT INSTALL \n   J2 (BUS OUT) MOLEX CONNECTOR. INSTEAD, INSTALL A 120 Ω THRU-HOLE RESISTOR ACROSS \n   PINS 4 AND 5 OF J2 (BUS OUT).\n\n2) ABSIS RS485 BUS SPECIFICATION\n   2.1) BUS IS HALF DUPLEX; TRANSMIT OR RECEIVE ONLY AT ANY GIVEN TIME.\n   2.2) PIN FUNCTION: R = DATA OUTPUT / D = DATA INPUT / DE HAS INTERNAL PULL-DOWN\n   (DRIVER DISABLED BY DEFAULT) / RE HAS INTERNAL PULL-UP (RECEIVER DISABLED BY DEFAULT).\n   2.3) CIRCUIT PROVIDES OPEN, SHORT, AND IDLE-BUS FAILSAFE OPERATION TO PREVENT ELECTRICAL\n   NOISE FROM BEING INTERPRETED AS VALID DATA.\n   2.4) THVD1410DR TRANSCEIVER OPERATES WITH TTL-LEVEL INPUTS. LOGIC HIGH: 2 V TO VCC /\n   LOGIC LOW: 0 V TO 0.8 V.\n   2.5) CAUTION: MAX DATA RATE DECREASES AS CABLE LENGTH INCREASES.\n\n3) POWER SYSTEM\n   3.1) ALE+ IS DESIGNED FOR NOM 12 V ABSIS BUS PWR. DO NOT APPLY 12 V TO VCC OR ANY\n   LOGIC/I/O SIGNAL.\n   3.2) U2 REGULATES THE 12 V BUS TO APPROX 7.3 V. U1 RAW IS SUPPLIED FROM THE +7.3 V\n   RAIL THRU D3.\n   3.3) D3 IS A SERIES SILICON RECTIFIER DIODE BETWEEN THE +7.3 V RAIL AND U1 RAW.\n   DO NOT BYPASS OR SHORT D3.\n   3.4) D3 PROVIDES REVERSE-CURRENT ISOLATION BETWEEN U1 RAW AND THE +7.3 V RAIL.\n   D3 IS NOT A 12 V CLAMP OR OVERVOLTAGE PROTECTION DEVICE.\n   3.5) DO NOT BACKFEED THE +7.3 V RAIL OR U1 VCC FROM EXT EQUIPMENT. USB PWR, WHEN USED,\n   SHALL ENTER THRU THE PROMICRO USB CONNECTOR.\n   3.6) F1 AND D2 ARE PART OF THE 12 V INPUT PROTECTION CIRCUIT. DO NOT BYPASS OR\n   SUBSTITUTE THESE DEVICES WITH JUMPERS DURING NORMAL OPERATION.\n   3.7) U1 VCC IS THE PROMICRO LOGIC SUPPLY RAIL. DO NOT USE VCC AS A SUBSTITUTE FOR\n   THE +7.3 V OR +12 V PWR RAILS.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 90.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6255b6d8-2584-4518-90ca-01ee46283941")
	)
	(text "4) I/O CONNECTORS\n   4.1) J8 AND J9 ARE UNKEYED 2X6, 2.54 MM GENERAL-PURPOSE I/O HEADERS. VERIFY PIN 1\n   ORIENTATION BEFORE CONNECTING HARNESS OR TEST EQUIPMENT.\n   4.2) J8 AND J9 I/O SIGNALS CONNECT DIRECTLY TO PROMICRO I/O PINS. EXT SIGNAL VOLTAGE\n   SHALL NOT EXCEED THE LOGIC SUPPLY VOLTAGE OF THE INSTALLED PROMICRO. I/O SIGNALS\n   ARE NOT 12 V TOLERANT.\n   4.3) DO NOT DRIVE J8 OR J9 I/O SIGNALS WHILE U1 IS UNPOWERED. EXT SIGNALS MAY BACKPOWER\n   U1 THRU THE MICROCONTROLLER INPUT PROTECTION CIRCUITRY.\n   4.4) ALL EXT DEVICES CONNECTED TO J8 OR J9 SHALL SHARE COMMON GND WITH ALE+ UNLESS\n   GALVANIC ISOLATION IS PROVIDED EXTERNALLY.\n   4.5) SIGNAL NAMES SDA_D2, SCL_D3, D4_A6, AND D6_A7 IDENTIFY MULTIPLEXED PROMICRO\n   FUNCTIONS. VERIFY FIRMWARE PIN ASSIGNMENT BEFORE CONNECTING EXT HARDWARE.\n   4.6) VCC AT THE I/O HEADERS IS A LOGIC SUPPLY AND SHALL NOT BE USED TO PWR\n   HIGH-CURRENT LOADS.\n   4.7) J8 AND J9 ARE INTENDED FOR SHORT, INTERNAL I/O CONNECTIONS. PROVIDE APPROPRIATE\n   LEVEL SHIFTING, ESD PROTECTION, TRANSIENT PROTECTION, OR ISOLATION FOR EXT OR\n   LONG-CABLE APPLICATIONS.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 143.002 61.468 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6641303b-ae5c-4c71-abdd-df80a09daab9")
	)
